From: Ryan Nelson <ryan@ryan.net>
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] target/sparc: flush replaced TTE as one range

Base: QEMU v8.2.2 (11aa0b1ff115b86160c4d37e7c37e6a6b13b77ea)

OpenIndiana boot profiling showed repeated per-8 KiB page invalidation from
replace_tlb_entry() dominating the sampled TCG vCPU cost for large SPARC TTEs.
Use QEMU's range helper so small mappings retain page-granular behavior while
ranges larger than the TCG TLB can select a single full flush.

This patch compiles as qemu-system-sparc64.  It has not yet passed the planned
OpenIndiana baseline/experimental A/B boot, storage, channel, or ZFS checks.
Do not treat it as a correctness-validated optimization.

diff --git a/target/sparc/ldst_helper.c b/target/sparc/ldst_helper.c
index 09066d5..1370049 100644
--- a/target/sparc/ldst_helper.c
+++ b/target/sparc/ldst_helper.c
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@ static void replace_tlb_entry(SparcTLBEntry *tlb,
                               uint64_t tlb_tag, uint64_t tlb_tte,
                               CPUSPARCState *env)
 {
-    target_ulong mask, size, va, offset;
+    target_ulong mask, size, va;
 
     /* flush page range if translation is valid */
     if (TTE_IS_VALID(tlb->tte)) {
@@ -135,9 +135,16 @@ static void replace_tlb_entry(SparcTLBEntry *tlb,
 
         va = tlb->tag & mask;
 
-        for (offset = 0; offset < size; offset += TARGET_PAGE_SIZE) {
-            tlb_flush_page(cs, va + offset);
-        }
+        /*
+         * Flush the complete mapping as one range.  In particular, avoid
+         * taking the TCG TLB lock and scanning the victim table once for
+         * every 8 KiB page in a large SPARC TTE.  The range helper retains
+         * page-granular behavior for small mappings and selects a single
+         * full flush when that is cheaper than walking the range.
+         */
+        tlb_flush_range_by_mmuidx(cs, va, size,
+                                  (1U << (MMU_PHYS_IDX + 1)) - 1,
+                                  TARGET_LONG_BITS);
     }
 
     tlb->tag = tlb_tag;
